### Phase 4: Transaction Control Language (TCL)
*TCL commands manage atomic operations to maintain data integrity during multi-step database changes.*
```sql
-- Disable autocommit to manually manage transactions
SET autocommit = 0;
-- Scenario: Processing an order and updating stock safely
-- 1. Start Transaction
START TRANSACTION;
-- Step A: Deduct inventory for an order
UPDATE products 
SET stock_quantity = stock_quantity - 1 
WHERE product_id = 2 AND stock_quantity >= 1;

-- Step B: Set a SAVEPOINT after stock deduction
SAVEPOINT stock_updated;

-- Step C: Log the agent transaction
INSERT INTO agent_logs (user_prompt, response_text, tokens_used) 
VALUES ('Purchase product 2', 'Stock deducted successfully', 150);

-- Step D: Test ROLLBACK to Savepoint (If logging failed or needed conditional undo)
-- ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT stock_updated;

-- Step E: Commit changes permanently to database
COMMIT;

-- Re-enable autocommit
SET autocommit = 1;

```
