### SQL Command Reference
| Category | Primary Commands | Core Function |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **DDL** (Data Definition Language) | `CREATE`, `ALTER`, `DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, `RENAME` | Defines and alters database schema structures. |
| **DML** (Data Manipulation Language) | `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE` | Modifies, adds, and removes table records. |
| **DQL** (Data Query Language) | `SELECT` | Filters, aggregates, and retrieves stored data. |
| **DCL** (Data Control Language) | `GRANT`, `REVOKE` | Controls user permissions and security access levels. |
| **TCL** (Transaction Control Language) | `COMMIT`, `ROLLBACK`, `SAVEPOINT` | Manages atomic operations and transactional integrity. |
